  { q: 'Is "unkindness of ravens" a real term?', a: 'Yes — "unkindness" is listed as a collective noun for ravens in historical and modern usage. It appears in sources as early as the 15th-century English hunting manuals. The origin is unclear; it may reflect ravens\' reputation as bad omens or their aggressive behaviour at carcasses.' },
  { q: 'Is "conspiracy of ravens" a real term?', a: '"Conspiracy" is a modern collective noun for ravens that has become widely used in popular writing and online sources. It is not documented in historical sources with the same antiquity as "unkindness". Both terms are used today, but "unkindness" has the stronger historical record.' },
